description:
FOUND DURING: module-structure review session, when the tracked JSONL was found to be 81 issues while the live Dolt DB held 99 (all 17 beads created that session were missing from the tracked file).

CAUSE: in Dolt mode (see .beads/metadata.json, backend=dolt, mode=embedded) the automatic flush goes to the local Dolt backup under .beads/backup/ (gitignored), NOT to the tracked .beads/issues.jsonl. That file is only written by an explicit bd export. AGENTS.md calls it a passive export; it is passive to the point of never updating on its own.

CORRECT FIX (not a git hook): bd 1.2.2 already exposes export config keys. Note the original ask was to wire this into the beads git hooks, which is the wrong mechanism on two counts: .git/hooks are not installed at all (bd hooks list reports all five as not installed), and .beads/hooks/* are bd-managed shims between BEGIN/END BEADS INTEGRATION markers that bd rewrites.

Relevant keys and current values (bd config show):
  export.auto      = false  (default)
  export.git-add   = false  (default)
  export.interval  = 60s    (default)
  export.path      = issues.jsonl

Proposed: bd config set export.auto true, and decide whether export.git-add true is wanted so the export is staged automatically. Then determine whether the setting persists in the Dolt DB (local-only, lost on a fresh clone) or in tracked .beads/config.yaml, and if it is DB-only, record it in config.yaml or AGENTS.md so another machine gets the same behaviour.

SECONDARY, same theme: bd 1.2.2 has no bd sync subcommand (unknown command "sync"), yet .beads/README.md still documents the pre-Dolt model ("Stored in .beads/issues.jsonl and synced like code", "Auto-syncs with your commits"), and AGENTS.md plus the bv instructions also reference bd sync. Update or ignore with a pointer, since that boilerplate is what made the current design look contradictory. There are also no refs/dolt/* refs and no git remote, consistent with AGENTS.md noting the repo is local-only.
